{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210734,"nonce":"QnExGyUhcFo9W+s2ZxWuxnNoApQ=","title":"hatch bundle merger left dedup'd transitive modules at first-installed position","message":"Fixed; see git log for the landing commit. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n**Symptom:** An example hatchfile that lists *both* `@hatch:game`\nand `@hatch:fsm` as path deps (each of which has\n`\"@hatch:events\" = \"0.2.2\"` in its own hatchfile) crashes at\nruntime with:\n\n```\nError: Null does not implement 'new()'\nNote 1: `Null` has no getter or method `new()`. Did you mean to call it with `()`?\nNote 2: stack trace:\n          at ensureInit_() (actions:363)\n          at update_(_,_) (actions)\n          at update_(_) (actions)\n          at run(_) (@hatch:game)\n```\n\n(or the equivalent at `fsm:694` when StateChart.build is the\nfirst user of EventEmitter).\n\n`EventEmitter` is `null` inside the importing module's scope.\n\n**Why (current hypothesis):** When the hatch builder walks\ntransitive deps, each path-dep recursively builds against the\nregistry copy of `@hatch:events`. The dep's bundle gets its\nmodules merged into the outer example bundle. But scoped names\n(`@hatch:events`) collide with bare names (`events`) the way\n`./css` vs `css` did before commit `78f0234`. Each path-dep's\nevents copy ends up at a slightly different bundled module\nname, so `find_imported_var_from(name, \"@hatch:events\")` from\nfsm's import line resolves against an entry that has no\n`EventEmitter` slot populated.\n\nThe earlier fix at `vm.rs:1796` normalises `./foo` / `../foo`\nbut doesn't handle the cross-package `@hatch:foo` ↔ bare-name\ncollision that arises when two path deps each carry the same\nregistry dep.\n\n**Adjacent symptom (likely same cause):**\n\n```\nhatch: dep '@hatch:json' bundled '@hatch:json'@unknown with bytes\nthat differ from another dep's copy — keeping the first-installed\n```\n\nThe warning surfaces during `hatch build` whenever any pair of\ndeps disagree on the bytes for a shared registry dep. The\n`@hatch:events` case doesn't even produce the warning yet\nbecause the bundled bytes match, but the *module-name keying*\nstill ends up split.\n\n**Reproduction:** `examples/game/fruit-slicer` originally\nlisted both `@hatch:game` (path) + `@hatch:fsm` (path) plus\nexplicit `@hatch:events = \"0.2.2\"` registry pin in its\nhatchfile. Drop in any `StateChart.build {|c| ... }` call from\nsetup and the first frame triggers the abort above.\n\n**Workaround used in `examples/game/fruit-slicer`:** drop\n`@hatch:fsm` from the deps, use an inline `_state` String for\nthe splash → loading → ready → playing → gameover transitions.\nThe chart-wiring pattern (loader signals → `chart.send`) is\ndocumented in `@hatch:assets/loader.wren`'s module header so\nthe canonical wiring story still exists in source for when\nthis lands.\n\n**Fix sketch:** when `compute_reachable_hatch_modules` (and the\nmatching var-resolution fallback) encounters an import like\n`@hatch:events`, also probe candidates of the form\n`events` (bare-name, in case the package was bundled under its\nentry filename rather than its scoped name). And during the\nhatch build merge, when multiple path-deps each carry the same\nscoped dep, dedupe by `(scoped-name, version)` keeping one\ncopy under the canonical scoped name.\n\n**Surrounding context:**\n\n- Recent fix `78f0234` (2026-05-11) — relative-import\n  normalisation `./foo` → `foo`.\n- Recent fix `9e7b48f` (2026-05-19) — `aot: normalize\n  relative-import source_path when binding to archive modules`.\n- The fixes covered relative-path imports but not scoped\n  registry-name vs bare-name dedup across nested deps.","files":null}]}